<section class="section page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="badge badge-primary">How It Works</span>
      <h1>Mirror a public website in three simple steps</h1>
      <p>From URL to ZIP — here is the whole flow.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">1</span>
        <h3>Enter Website URL</h3>
        <p>Paste the address of a publicly accessible website you want to mirror.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">2</span>
        <h3>Download Website Resources</h3>
        <p>We mirror the HTML pages and linked static resources.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">3</span>
        <h3>Download Your ZIP Archive</h3>
        <p>The collected files are packaged into a ZIP archive, available for a limited time before it is removed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container container-narrow">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What happens behind the scenes</h2>
      <p>
        Once you submit a public URL, our server validates that it is a real http(s)
        address and that it does not point to a private network, localhost or a
        cloud metadata endpoint. It then runs the GNU Wget engine to mirror the page
        and its linked assets.
      </p>
      <p>
        You see live progress — the actual Wget output and a running file count —
        over a Socket.IO connection. When the download finishes, the files are
        compressed into a ZIP archive stored in a private folder.
      </p>
      <h2>ZIP retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Archives are stored temporarily and are <strong>deleted automatically after
        a successful download</strong> or after the configured retention period
        (24 hours by default). They are never served as public static files, so you
        must download your ZIP before it expires.
      </p>
      <h2>Limitations</h2>
      <p>
        Only publicly accessible content is mirrored. Dynamic content generated at
        runtime, resources behind authentication, and assets blocked by robots.txt
        may be missing. We never claim complete offline functionality for dynamic
        websites.
      </p>
    </div>
    {{> ad-unit adSlot="1234567892"}}
  </div>
</section>
